    {
      "id": "claim_5b2f371af2e749039c2db20441710633",
      "statement": "align_citations and PreparedCitationCorpus.align accept a backend argument with three values: \"auto\" (default, try Rust then fall back), \"python\" (force SmithWatermanAligner), and \"rust\" (require RustSmithWatermanAligner, raise on construction failure); on the 0.5.0 bindings, rust_tokenize_and_prepare takes normalize_numbers/normalize_percent/normalize_currency as required keyword-only args and both Rust citation builders require query_stopword_ids and accept optional alias_remap, keyword-only in rust_build_citations_fast.",
      "evidence": [
